    "narrative": "The **Zurich Zebras** face a complex slate today, but the primary engine for our offensive output is clearly **Pete Crow-Armstrong**. With a score of 78.29, he stands as our elite play; his efficiency is driven by a favorable matchup against Michael King (4.39 xERA) and, crucially, his aggressive base-stealing profile which is vital for our pursuit of the SB category. While **Trea Turner** remains a roster staple, he draws the toughest assignment of the day against an elite arm in Chris Sale (2.79 xERA). Despite the SP skill penalty, **Trea Turner** maintains a 54.65 score due to his high-leverage leadoff spot and platoon advantage, making him a high-floor play even against a Cy Young-caliber performance. **Yordan Alvarez** faces a difficult L/L matchup that suppresses his ceiling to 46.83, yet his xwOBA profile remains too elite to consider benching, even with the SP skill penalty.\n\nOur bench strategy is defined by the absence of several key contributors. We are managing the unfortunate absence of **Colt Keith** due to his IL designation, while **Junior Caminero**, **Christian Yelich**, and **Kazuma Okamoto** are unavailable due to team off-days. Consequently, **Chase Meidroth** (41.04) and **Caleb Durbin** (42.37) round out the starting nine. **Caleb Durbin** is a marginal start pending official lineup confirmation, but his ability to contribute as a speed threat keeps him slightly ahead of our depth chart options like **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** or **Carson Benge**. We are monitoring the status of **Gary Sanchez**, **Lars Nootbaar**, **Casey Schmitt**, **Dillon Dingler**, **Josh Smith**, **Jacob Gonzalez**, **Hector Rodriguez**, **Luis Pena**, and **Pedro Ramirez** closely, though they remain on the sidelines today as the rotation optimizer prioritizes the high-sprint-speed profile of our active lineup to secure the scarcest category points.",
